{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 26, :comments ["<b>The blessings of your father prevailed, etc.</b> The blessings with which the Holy One, blessed be He, blessed me prevailed and overpowered the blessings with which my parents blessed me." "<b>To the desire of the everlasting hills.</b> Because my blessings prevailed to the ends of the borders of the everlasting hills — for He gave me a bursting blessing without bounds, reaching to the four corners of the world, as it says ״וּפָרַצְתָּ יָמָּה וָקֵדְמָה וגו׳״ — which He did not say to Abraham our father and to Isaac. To Abraham He said ״שָׂא נָא עֵינֶיךָ וּרְאֵה צָפֹנָה וגו׳ כִּי אֶת כָּל הָאָרֶץ אֲשֶׁר אַתָּה רֹאֶה לְךָ אֶתְּנֶנָּה״, and He showed him nothing but the land of Israel alone. To Isaac He said ״לְךָ וּלְזַרְעֲךָ אֶתֵּן אֶת כָּל הָאֲרָצֹת הָאֵל וַהֲקִימֹתִי אֶת הַשְּׁבֻעָה וגו׳״. And this is what Isaiah said (Isaiah 58): ״וְהַאֲכַלְתִּיךָ נַחֲלַת יַעֲקֹב אָבִיךָ״ — and he did not say the heritage of Abraham." "<b>My parents.</b> A term of pregnancy — for they conceived me in my mother's womb, as in ״הֹרָה גָבֶר״ (Job 3)." "<b>To the desire.</b> To the borders, as in ״וְהִתְאַוִּיתֶם לָכֶם לִגְבוּל קֵדְמָה״ (Numbers 34), ״תְּתָאוּ לָבֹא חֲמָת״ (there)." "<b>Desire.</b> אשׁמו״לץ בְּלַעַז — thus Menahem ben Saruk composed it. And Onkelos translated תַּאֲוַת עוֹלָם — a term of desire and coveting; and גִּבְעוֹת — a term of the heights of the earth whose desirability their mother established and assigned them to receive." "<b>May they be.</b> All of them upon the head of Yosef." "<b>The nazir of his brothers.</b> פְּרִישָׁא דַּאֲחוֹהִי — that he separated himself from his brothers, as in ״וְיִנָּזְרוּ מִקָּדְשֵׁי בְנֵי יִשְׂרָאֵל״ (Leviticus 22), ״נָזֹרוּ אָחוֹר״ (Isaiah 1)."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 49, :notes {4 "The la'az אשׁמו״לץ corresponds to Old French açmolez / essmolez, meaning 'desire, longing'."}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:04:26.705929791Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}